IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employee`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- day one of a job: the NES as a floor, the information statements, and the records.
--
-- SEAT: the employee. "Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement? Can my contract give me less
-- than the NES? What records must my employer keep about me?" Every question below is phrased as the employee would
-- ask it, on facts the employee could state. The employer's side of the same rules is asked in fwa-seat-employer.l4,
-- which calls the rules here and restates none of them.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. s 44 (an employer must not contravene the NES); s 60 (the NES apply to national system
-- employees); s 61 (the NES are minimum standards that cannot be displaced; the matters they cover); s 125 (giving a new
-- employee the Fair Work Information Statement), with s 61(2)(j) (that duty is itself part of the NES); s 125B (giving a
-- casual the Casual Employment Information Statement: at the start, at 6 months, at 12 months and each 12 months after,
-- with the small business exceptions); s 333K (giving the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement, the third
-- statement a new employee can be owed on day one); s 535 (making and keeping employee records for 7 years), with
-- regs 3.31 to 3.40 and 3.42 of the Fair Work Regulations 2009 (the kinds of record, their form, and the employee's
-- right to inspect and copy them); s 557C (an employer that kept no record must disprove the allegation).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 73, compilation date 7 July 2026 (register id C2026C00355), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt. Regulations: Fair Work Regulations 2009 (F2009L02356), Compilation
-- No. 57, compilation date 1 October 2026 (register id F2026C00996), as deposited at
-- ../../../fair-work-regulations-2009/registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt -- regs 2.02, 2.02A (how a statement may
-- be given: read, not encoded, see NOTES.md), 3.31 to 3.40, 3.42.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The contents of the statements themselves (s 124(2), s 125A(2), s 333J(2), reg 2.01: duties of the Fair
-- Work Ombudsman); the manner of giving a statement (regs 2.02, 2.02A: any manner is allowed, reg 2.02(7)); s 55 and
-- s 56 (what an award or enterprise agreement may say about the NES: this module asks about the employment CONTRACT);
-- the NES provisions that let an employer and employee agree on something (ss 62, 64, 94, 101 and so on) are asked
-- as a fact, not worked out; the s 15A casual employee test (asked as a fact); the s 333E limits on fixed term
-- contracts; reg 3.41 (records on a transfer of business); reg 3.43 (where records are kept; interviews); reg 3.44
-- (correcting records); civil penalty amounts; inspectors' powers (Part 5-2).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18; no REFUSE: a case outside the Act's reach answers an explicit "not covered" value. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- day one: the employee's questions`

§§ `ss 44, 60, 61 -- the National Employment Standards as a floor`

-- s 61(2): "The minimum standards relate to the following matters: (a) maximum weekly hours (Division 3); (b) requests
-- for flexible working arrangements (Division 4); (ba) casual employment (Division 4A); (c) parental leave and related
-- entitlements (Division 5); (d) annual leave (Division 6); (e) personal/carer's leave, compassionate leave and paid
-- family and domestic violence leave (Division 7); (f) community service leave (Division 8); (g) long service leave
-- (Division 9); (h) public holidays (Division 10); (ha) superannuation contributions (Division 10A); (i) notice of
-- termination and redundancy pay (Division 11); (j) Fair Work Information Statement (Division 12)."
-- s 61(3): "Divisions 3 to 12 constitute the National Employment Standards."
DECLARE `NES matter` IS ONE OF
    `maximum weekly hours (Division 3)`
    `requests for flexible working arrangements (Division 4)`
    `casual employment (Division 4A)`
    `parental leave and related entitlements (Division 5)`
    `annual leave (Division 6)`
    `personal/carer's leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave (Division 7)`
    `community service leave (Division 8)`
    `long service leave (Division 9)`
    `public holidays (Division 10)`
    `superannuation contributions (Division 10A)`
    `notice of termination and redundancy pay (Division 11)`
    `the Fair Work Information Statement and the Casual Employment Information Statement (Division 12)`

@export What are the National Employment Standards, the minimum my employer must give me (s 61(2))?
GIVETH A LIST OF `NES matter`
DECIDE `What are the National Employment Standards` IS
    LIST `maximum weekly hours (Division 3)`,
         `requests for flexible working arrangements (Division 4)`,
         `casual employment (Division 4A)`,
         `parental leave and related entitlements (Division 5)`,
         `annual leave (Division 6)`,
         `personal/carer's leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave (Division 7)`,
         `community service leave (Division 8)`,
         `long service leave (Division 9)`,
         `public holidays (Division 10)`,
         `superannuation contributions (Division 10A)`,
         `notice of termination and redundancy pay (Division 11)`,
         `the Fair Work Information Statement and the Casual Employment Information Statement (Division 12)`

-- s 61(1): "This Part sets minimum standards that apply to the employment of employees which cannot be displaced, even
-- if an enterprise agreement includes terms of the kind referred to in subsection 55(5)."
-- s 60: "In this Part, employee means a national system employee, and employer means a national system employer."
-- s 44: "An employer must not contravene a provision of the National Employment Standards."
-- The Act has no provision on what an employment CONTRACT may say about the NES (ss 55 and 56 deal only with awards and
-- enterprise agreements). The answer follows from s 61(1) and s 44 together: a contract term that gives less than the
-- NES cannot displace them, and an employer that acts on it contravenes s 44. Some NES provisions themselves let the
-- employer and employee agree something (for example s 64, averaging of hours for an award/agreement free employee,
-- "agree in writing"; s 94, cashing out annual leave); whether a term is such an agreement is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `What the contract term does` IS ONE OF
    `it gives less than the NES on an NES matter`
    `it gives the same as the NES, or more`
    `it is an agreement that an NES provision itself allows`

DECLARE `Where the contract term stands` IS ONE OF
    `the NES apply in full: the term cannot displace them (s 61(1)), and acting on it would contravene s 44`
    `the term can operate: it does not undercut the NES`
    `not covered: the NES apply only to a national system employee (s 60)`

GIVEN `national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term` IS A `What the contract term does`
GIVETH A `Where the contract term stands`
`the NES against a contract term` MEANS
    IF NOT `national system employee`
    THEN `not covered: the NES apply only to a national system employee (s 60)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the term`
         WHEN `it gives less than the NES on an NES matter`
              THEN `the NES apply in full: the term cannot displace them (s 61(1)), and acting on it would contravene s 44`
         WHEN `it gives the same as the NES, or more` THEN `the term can operate: it does not undercut the NES`
         WHEN `it is an agreement that an NES provision itself allows` THEN `the term can operate: it does not undercut the NES`

@export Can my employment contract give me less than the National Employment Standards (ss 44, 60, 61)?
GIVEN `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee (an employee of a national system employer, such as a company; not on an unpaid vocational placement)
      `what the term does` IS A `What the contract term does` @desc What the contract term (for example a probation clause) does compared with the National Employment Standards
GIVETH A `Where the contract term stands`
DECIDE `Can my contract give me less than the NES` IS
    `the NES against a contract term` `I am a national system employee` `what the term does`

-- s 44, through s 60: the duty binds a national system employer to a national system employee.
GIVEN `national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an NES requirement was not met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer has contravened s 44` IF
        `national system employee`
    AND `an NES requirement was not met`

@export Has my employer contravened the National Employment Standards (s 44)?
GIVEN `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee
      `my employer has not given me something an NES provision requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has failed to give you something a National Employment Standard requires (leave, notice, a statement, and so on)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer contravened the NES` IF
    `the employer has contravened s 44` `I am a national system employee` `my employer has not given me something an NES provision requires`

§§ `s 125 -- the Fair Work Information Statement`

-- s 125(1): "An employer must give each employee the Fair Work Information Statement before, or as soon as practicable
-- after, the employee starts employment." (2): "Subsection (1) does not require the employer to give the employee the
-- Statement more than once in any 12 months." Note: "This is relevant if the employer employs the employee more than
-- once in the 12 months." READING: (2) is applied to a re-employment within 12 months of the last statement.
GIVEN `national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given it in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must give the Fair Work Information Statement` IF
        `national system employee`
    AND (NOT `given it in the 12 months before this start`)

@export Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement, before or as soon as practicable after I start (s 125)?
GIVEN `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee
      `this employer gave me the statement in the 12 months before I started this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have worked for this employer before: whether they gave you the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this job started
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement` IF
    `the employer must give the Fair Work Information Statement` `I am a national system employee` `this employer gave me the statement in the 12 months before I started this time`

-- s 61(2)(j) and (3): Division 12, which holds s 125, is part of the NES; so not giving the statement is a contravention
-- of s 44 itself. "As soon as practicable" is a judgment, asked conditionally.
@export Has my employer contravened the NES by not giving me the Fair Work Information Statement (ss 44, 61(2)(j), 125)?
GIVEN `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee
      `this employer gave me the statement in the 12 months before I started this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have worked for this employer before: whether they gave you the statement in the 12 months before this job started
      `I have been given the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has given you the Fair Work Information Statement for this job (in person, by post, by email or a link to it)
      `if as soon as practicable after I started has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time that was "as soon as practicable" after you started has already passed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer contravened the NES over the Fair Work Information Statement` IF
    `the employer has contravened s 44`
        `I am a national system employee`
        (    `the employer must give the Fair Work Information Statement` `I am a national system employee` `this employer gave me the statement in the 12 months before I started this time`
         AND (NOT `I have been given the statement`)
         AND `if as soon as practicable after I started has passed`)

§§ `s 125B -- the Casual Employment Information Statement (only if you are a casual)`

-- s 125B(1): "An employer must give a casual employee the Casual Employment Information Statement: (a) before, or as
-- soon as practicable after, the employee starts employment as a casual employee with the employer; and (b) as soon as
-- practicable after the employee has been employed by the employer for a period of 6 months ...; and (c) as soon as
-- practicable after the following: (i) the employee has been employed by the employer for a period of 12 months ...;
-- (ii) the end of any subsequent period of 12 months for which the employee is employed by the employer."
-- (2): "paragraph (1)(b) and subparagraph (1)(c)(ii) do not apply if at the time ... the employer is a small business
-- employer." (3): the section does not, "apart from the operation of paragraph (1)(b)", require the statement "more
-- than once in any 12 months" -- READING, as for s 125(2): applied to a re-employment at the start.
-- s 23(1): a small business employer has fewer than 15 employees (the rule in fwa-employee.l4).
-- "Casual employee" (s 15A) is a multi-factor test, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Casual statement occasion` IS ONE OF
    `starting as a casual`
    `6 months after starting`
    `12 months after starting`
    `the end of each further 12 months`

GIVEN `casual employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occasion` IS A `Casual statement occasion`
      `employees counted under s 23 at that time` IS A NUMBER
      `given it in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must give the Casual Employment Information Statement` IF
        `casual employee`
    AND `national system employee`
    AND CONSIDER `the occasion`
        WHEN `starting as a casual` THEN NOT `given it in the 12 months before this start`
        WHEN `6 months after starting` THEN NOT `my employer is a small business employer` `employees counted under s 23 at that time`
        WHEN `12 months after starting` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the end of each further 12 months` THEN NOT `my employer is a small business employer` `employees counted under s 23 at that time`

@export Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement at this point (s 125B)?
GIVEN `I am a casual employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee: no firm advance commitment to continuing and indefinite work, and a casual loading or casual rate (s 15A)
      `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee
      `the point I have reached` IS A `Casual statement occasion` @desc Which point you have reached with this employer
      `how many employees my employer has` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees your employer has at that point, counting yourself and any casuals only if they are employed regularly and systematically (s 23)
      `this employer gave me the statement in the 12 months before I started this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have worked for this employer before: whether they gave you this statement in the 12 months before this job started
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` IF
    `the employer must give the Casual Employment Information Statement`
        `I am a casual employee` `I am a national system employee` `the point I have reached`
        `how many employees my employer has` `this employer gave me the statement in the 12 months before I started this time`

§§ `s 333K -- the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement (only if your contract has an end date)`

-- s 333K: "If a person enters into a contract of employment that includes a term that provides the contract will
-- terminate at the end of an identifiable period ..., the person must, before, or as soon as practicable after, the
-- contract is entered into, give the employee the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement." Not part of the NES (it is
-- in Part 2-9); a civil remedy provision of its own. Part 2-9 applies to national system employment (s 60 is not the
-- source; the Act's general reach is): READING, so it is asked of a national system employee here.
GIVEN `national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract ends at the end of an identifiable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must give the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement` IF
        `national system employee`
    AND `the contract ends at the end of an identifiable period`

@export Must my employer give me the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement (s 333K)?
GIVEN `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee
      `my contract ends at the end of a set period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract says it ends at the end of an identifiable period (a date, a task or a season), even if it can also end earlier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement` IF
    `the employer must give the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement` `I am a national system employee` `my contract ends at the end of a set period`

§§ `ss 125, 125B(1)(a), 333K -- everything owed on day one`

-- The three statements an employee can be owed before, or as soon as practicable after, starting. Pay slips (s 536,
-- in fwa-employee.l4) come with the first pay, not on day one.
DECLARE `Day-one statement` IS ONE OF
    `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`
    `the Casual Employment Information Statement (s 125B(1)(a))`
    `the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement (s 333K)`

DECLARE `Day-one answer` IS ONE OF
    `these statements` HAS `the statements` IS A LIST OF `Day-one statement`
    `not covered: these duties are owed only to a national system employee`

GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement` IS A `Day-one statement`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Day-one statement`
`the statement if` MEANS IF `b` THEN LIST `the statement` ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `casual employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract ends at the end of an identifiable period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before this start` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Day-one answer`
`the day-one statements` MEANS
    IF NOT `national system employee`
    THEN `not covered: these duties are owed only to a national system employee`
    ELSE `these statements` (concat OF LIST
            (`the statement if`
                (`the employer must give the Fair Work Information Statement` `national system employee` `given the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this start`)
                `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`),
            (`the statement if`
                (`the employer must give the Casual Employment Information Statement` `casual employee` `national system employee` `starting as a casual` 0 `given the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before this start`)
                `the Casual Employment Information Statement (s 125B(1)(a))`),
            (`the statement if`
                (`the employer must give the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement` `national system employee` `the contract ends at the end of an identifiable period`)
                `the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement (s 333K)`))
-- The 0 above is a placeholder for the s 23 count: the rule reads it only at 6 months and after each further 12, never
-- at the start.

@export Which information statements must my employer give me when I start (ss 125, 125B(1)(a), 333K)?
GIVEN `I am a national system employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a national system employee
      `I am a casual employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you start as a casual employee (s 15A)
      `my contract ends at the end of a set period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract says it ends at the end of an identifiable period
      `this employer gave me the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before I started this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have worked for this employer before: whether they gave you the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before this job started
      `this employer gave me the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before I started this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have worked for this employer before as a casual: whether they gave you the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before this job started
GIVETH A `Day-one answer`
DECIDE `Which statements must I be given when I start` IS
    `the day-one statements`
        `I am a national system employee` `I am a casual employee` `my contract ends at the end of a set period`
        `this employer gave me the Fair Work Information Statement in the 12 months before I started this time`
        `this employer gave me the Casual Employment Information Statement in the 12 months before I started this time`

§§ `s 535, regs 3.31-3.40 -- the records my employer must keep about me`

-- s 535(1): "An employer must make, and keep for 7 years, employee records of the kind prescribed by the regulations in
-- relation to each of its employees." (2): the records must be in any prescribed form and include any prescribed
-- information.
-- Reg 3.32: always -- "(a) the employer's name; (b) the employee's name; (c) whether the employee's employment is
-- full-time or part-time; (d) whether ... permanent, temporary or casual; (e) the date on which the employee's
-- employment began; and (f) ... the Australian Business Number (if any) of the employer."
-- Reg 3.33(1): always -- "(a) the rate of remuneration ...; (b) the gross and net amounts ...; (c) any deductions".
-- Reg 3.33(2): "a casual or irregular part-time employee who is guaranteed a rate of pay set by reference to a period
-- of time worked" -- the hours worked. (3): an incentive-based payment, bonus, loading, penalty rate or other allowance
-- or separately identifiable entitlement -- its details.
-- Reg 3.34: "if a penalty rate or loading ... must be paid for overtime hours actually worked" -- the overtime hours
-- each day, or when overtime started and ceased.
-- Reg 3.35: a written agreement to average hours -- a copy.
-- Reg 3.36(1): "if an employee is entitled to leave" -- leave taken and the balance. (2) leave cashed out by agreement
-- -- a copy of the agreement, the rate, and when paid.
-- Reg 3.37: "if an employer is required to make superannuation contributions" -- amounts, period, dates, fund, and the
-- basis of liability including the employee's choice of fund and its date.
-- Reg 3.38: an individual flexibility arrangement -- a copy, and of any notice or agreement ending it.
-- Reg 3.39: a guarantee of annual earnings (s 330) -- the guarantee, and the date of any revocation.
-- Reg 3.40: termination -- how it ended (consent, notice, summarily, or otherwise) and who ended it.
DECLARE `Employee record` IS ONE OF
    `names, full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or casual, start date, and the employer's ABN if any (reg 3.32)`
    `the rate of pay, gross and net amounts paid, and deductions (reg 3.33(1))`
    `the hours worked (reg 3.33(2))`
    `details of each incentive payment, bonus, loading, penalty rate or allowance (reg 3.33(3))`
    `the overtime hours worked each day, or when overtime started and stopped (reg 3.34)`
    `a copy of the written agreement to average hours (reg 3.35)`
    `leave taken and the leave balance (reg 3.36(1))`
    `a copy of the agreement to cash out leave, the rate, and when it was paid (reg 3.36(2))`
    `superannuation contributions: amounts, period, dates, fund, and why they were owed, including the fund choice and its date (reg 3.37)`
    `a copy of the individual flexibility arrangement, and of any notice or agreement ending it (reg 3.38)`
    `the guarantee of annual earnings, and the date of any revocation (reg 3.39)`
    `how the employment ended and who ended it (reg 3.40)`

GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record` IS AN `Employee record`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Employee record`
`the record if` MEANS IF `b` THEN LIST `the record` ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `casual or irregular part-time and paid by time worked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to a bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive payment or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty rate or loading is payable for overtime worked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a written agreement to average hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave has been cashed out by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `superannuation contributions are required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an individual flexibility arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a guarantee of annual earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Employee record`
`the records required` MEANS
    concat OF LIST
        (LIST `names, full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or casual, start date, and the employer's ABN if any (reg 3.32)`,
              `the rate of pay, gross and net amounts paid, and deductions (reg 3.33(1))`),
        (`the record if` `casual or irregular part-time and paid by time worked` `the hours worked (reg 3.33(2))`),
        (`the record if` `entitled to a bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive payment or allowance` `details of each incentive payment, bonus, loading, penalty rate or allowance (reg 3.33(3))`),
        (`the record if` `a penalty rate or loading is payable for overtime worked` `the overtime hours worked each day, or when overtime started and stopped (reg 3.34)`),
        (`the record if` `there is a written agreement to average hours` `a copy of the written agreement to average hours (reg 3.35)`),
        (`the record if` `entitled to leave` `leave taken and the leave balance (reg 3.36(1))`),
        (`the record if` `leave has been cashed out by agreement` `a copy of the agreement to cash out leave, the rate, and when it was paid (reg 3.36(2))`),
        (`the record if` `superannuation contributions are required` `superannuation contributions: amounts, period, dates, fund, and why they were owed, including the fund choice and its date (reg 3.37)`),
        (`the record if` `there is an individual flexibility arrangement` `a copy of the individual flexibility arrangement, and of any notice or agreement ending it (reg 3.38)`),
        (`the record if` `there is a guarantee of annual earnings` `the guarantee of annual earnings, and the date of any revocation (reg 3.39)`),
        (`the record if` `the employment has ended` `how the employment ended and who ended it (reg 3.40)`)

@export What records must my employer make and keep about me (s 535, regs 3.32-3.40)?
GIVEN `I am casual or irregular part-time, paid by the hour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual or irregular part-time employee guaranteed a rate of pay by reference to time worked
      `I am entitled to a bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive payment or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to any bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive-based payment or other allowance
      `I get a penalty rate or loading for overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a penalty rate or loading must be paid for overtime hours you actually work
      `I have agreed in writing to average my hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer have agreed in writing to average your hours of work
      `I am entitled to leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to any leave (paid or unpaid)
      `I have cashed out leave by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer have agreed to cash out some accrued leave
      `my employer must pay super for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is required to make superannuation contributions for you
      `I have an individual flexibility arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have agreed an individual flexibility arrangement in writing
      `I have a guarantee of annual earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has given you a guarantee of annual earnings (s 330)
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has ended
GIVETH A LIST OF `Employee record`
DECIDE `What records must my employer keep about me` IS
    `the records required`
        `I am casual or irregular part-time, paid by the hour`
        `I am entitled to a bonus, loading, penalty rate, incentive payment or allowance`
        `I get a penalty rate or loading for overtime`
        `I have agreed in writing to average my hours`
        `I am entitled to leave`
        `I have cashed out leave by agreement`
        `my employer must pay super for me`
        `I have an individual flexibility arrangement`
        `I have a guarantee of annual earnings`
        `my employment has ended`

-- s 535(1): "keep for 7 years". READING: the 7 years run from when the record is made (the Act does not say from
-- when; reg 3.41(6) supports it, treating a transferred record as made when the old employer made it).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years records must be kept` MEANS 7

@export For how many years must my employer keep my employee records (s 535(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years must my employer keep my records` IS `the years records must be kept`

GIVEN `years since the record was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record may be discarded` IF
    `years since the record was made` AT LEAST `the years records must be kept`

-- Reg 3.31(1): "(a) a record in a legible form and in the English language; (b) a record in a form that is readily
-- accessible to an inspector."
GIVEN `legible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `readily accessible to an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record is in the prescribed form` IF
        `legible`
    AND `in English`
    AND `readily accessible to an inspector`

-- Reg 3.42(1): the employer "must make a copy of an employee record available for inspection and copying on request by
-- the employee or former employee". (3) If kept at the premises where the employee works or worked: "(a) make the
-- copy available at the premises within 3 business days after receiving the request; or (b) post a copy ... within 14
-- days after receiving the request." (4) Otherwise, "as soon as practicable after receiving the request": make it
-- available at the premises, or post it.
DECLARE `Time to produce a record` IS ONE OF
    `within 3 business days at the workplace, or posted within 14 days (reg 3.42(3))`
    `as soon as practicable, at the workplace or by post (reg 3.42(4))`

GIVEN `kept at the premises where the employee works or worked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time to produce a record`
`the time to produce a record` MEANS
    IF `kept at the premises where the employee works or worked`
    THEN `within 3 business days at the workplace, or posted within 14 days (reg 3.42(3))`
    ELSE `as soon as practicable, at the workplace or by post (reg 3.42(4))`

@export How quickly must my employer let me inspect and copy my employee records once I ask (reg 3.42)?
GIVEN `my records are kept where I work or worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer keeps your records at the premises where you work (or worked)
GIVETH A `Time to produce a record`
DECIDE `How quickly must I be shown my records` IS
    `the time to produce a record` `my records are kept where I work or worked`

§§ `s 557C -- if my employer kept no records (only if you are claiming against your employer)`

-- s 557C(1): in proceedings about a contravention of a provision in (3) -- s 44 (the NES), s 45 (an award), s 50 (an
-- enterprise agreement), s 280 (a workplace determination), s 293 (a national minimum wage order), s 305 (an equal
-- remuneration order), s 323(1) and (3) (how and how often I am paid), s 325(1) (unreasonable requirements to spend or
-- pay) -- if the employer was required by s 535(1) or (2) to make and keep a record, or by the regulations under
-- s 535(3) to make one available, or by s 536 to give a pay slip, about the matter, and failed to, "the employer has the
-- burden of disproving the allegation". (2): not "if the employer provides a reasonable excuse" -- a judgment of the
-- court, asked conditionally.
GIVEN `the claim is under a provision listed in s 557C(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record or pay slip was required about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to make, keep, show or give it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if the court accepts the employer's reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must disprove the allegation` IF
        `the claim is under a provision listed in s 557C(3)`
    AND `a record or pay slip was required about the matter`
    AND `the employer failed to make, keep, show or give it`
    AND (NOT `if the court accepts the employer's reasonable excuse`)

@export If my employer did not keep the records, must my employer disprove what I allege (s 557C)?
GIVEN `my claim is about the NES, an award, an agreement, the minimum wage, or how I was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is that your employer contravened the NES, a modern award, an enterprise agreement, a workplace determination, a national minimum wage or equal remuneration order, the rules on how and how often you are paid, or the ban on unreasonable requirements to spend or pay money
      `my employer had to keep a record or give a pay slip about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law required your employer to make and keep a record, let you inspect one, or give you a pay slip, about the matter you allege
      `my employer did not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer failed to do so
      `if the court accepts my employer's reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court accepts a reasonable excuse from your employer for the failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer disprove what I allege` IF
    `the employer must disprove the allegation`
        `my claim is about the NES, an award, an agreement, the minimum wage, or how I was paid`
        `my employer had to keep a record or give a pay slip about it`
        `my employer did not`
        `if the court accepts my employer's reasonable excuse`
